<header class="page-head"><h1>Accessibility</h1></header>
<div class="prose">
<p>This site aims toward WCAG 2.2 AA. Its reading pages use semantic headings and landmarks, keyboard-operable links and disclosures, visible focus, reduced-motion styles, and HTML content that remains available without JavaScript.</p>
<p>Search, copying, and graphical map controls use JavaScript. The source text and static relationship lists remain available independently. The mobile menu remains expanded when JavaScript is disabled.</p>
<h2>What is checked</h2>
<p>The release suite checks selected public routes with automated accessibility rules, along with browser interactions and internal links. The September 17 audit also checks narrow-screen reflow and keyboard navigation for the revised reading and information pages. These checks support improvement; they do not establish complete WCAG conformance.</p>
<h2>Report a barrier</h2>
<p>Open a <a href="https://github.com/The-Interdependency/The-Interdependency.github.io/issues">website issue</a> with the page URL, the task you were trying to complete, and the browser or assistive technology involved if you wish to share it. Technical diagnosis is optional.</p>
<p><strong>hmmm:</strong> a comprehensive manual screen-reader review and testing with disabled users remain outstanding. Broader design practices and their sources are in <a href="/about-the-site/">About the site</a>.</p>
</div>
